# Aston Martin V12 Vanquish coupe, 2001-2007.
#
# The Ian Callum Newport Pagnell flagship: the 6.0-litre V12, the long low
# carbon-fibre body, the pronounced front splitter and the quad exhausts.
# 1,503 standard cars built before the Vanquish S of 2004; the S is a trim
# and power variant and is not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_Vanquish
#
# Dimensions 4.665 x 1.923 x 1.318 m, wheelbase 2.690 m.
#
# Shape reference: a silver 2004 car in a 30-35 degree front three-quarter
# (there is NO true side elevation in the pack), a silver 2001 car at Gaydon
# in front three-quarter, and the same car in rear three-quarter. The flank is
# estimated from the three views and the published dimensions; the limitation
# is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (c). Stronsay Silver, Derwent Green, Mendip Blue and Chiltern
# Green are documented in a commercial Aston Martin paint-code compilation for
# 2001-03; it is not a brochure and the full range is grade (d). Weights 3, 3,
# 2, 2, total 10, provisional.
#
# Speed 305 km/h. Comfort 78/447, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 78. Class 4.
# Dates are road presence: 2001 intro, retires staggered 2022-2025.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-vanquish.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-vanquish.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-vanquish/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear lamp shapes break at the corners and the
# plate recess is too rounded. There is no true side reference, so the flank
# is estimated. At 128 px the long low body, splitter, quad exhausts and V12
# proportions read as a Vanquish.


obj=citycar
